   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "Whether atomicity across the two reads in listdescriptors was intended now that they are read under two separate locks",
   "quote": "One subtle difference is that the descriptor metadata and descriptor string are now read under two separate locks instead of one caller-held lock. I don\u2019t see an issue because descriptor state should not normally change concurrently here, but I wanted to double-check that no atomicity across these two reads was intended.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2026-06-17",
    "by": "w0xlt",
    "id": "rc:3431882390",
    "quote": "Yes, I also think it is safe because listdescriptors holds wallet->cs_wallet across both calls."
   },
   "status_note": "author confirmed listdescriptors holds cs_wallet across both calls",
   "type": "question",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35444#discussion_r3385370769"
  },
